Lumen OS: A2DP SBC fed at 48 kHz and resampled to 44.1 kHz (Play 6 base only).

The XGIMI Play 6 audio HAL (audio.primary.mt5889) plays A2DP itself: a loopback copies its 48 kHz DSP output into
the Bluetooth stream and never resamples, while speakers often take SBC at 44.1 kHz only (the owner's Yandex
Station closes a 48 kHz SBC stream right after it starts). The music played about 8 % slow and skipped ahead every
few seconds (owner 2026-10-24). Now SBC at 44.1 kHz reports a 48 kHz PCM stream to the audio HAL, the SBC encoder
is fed at 48 kHz and a2dp_sbc_read_feeding resamples it with a new down-sampler (linear interpolation; the AOSP
up-sampler emits at least one sample per input and cannot lower the rate).

